          "filename": "Sepahsalar-e Azam-e Tonekaboni.jpg",
          "caption": "Mohammad Vali Khan, Sepahsālār-e Azam-e Tonekāboni (his family later adopted the family name Khalatbari), leader of the constitutionalist revolutionary forces from Iran's northern provinces of Gilan and Mazandaran. He was the first to arrive in Tehran and liberate the city from the Royalist forces. He became Minister of Defence in the first constitutionalist government following dethroning of Mohammad-Ali Shah Qajar in 1909. He subsequently became Iran's Prime Minister, holding this post between October 1909 and July 1910.",
